.el .ds Aq '
.TH iron-vault-approver-add 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-approver\-add \- Enroll another approval signer. The service shows what changes, asks for the approval passphrase of an approver already pinned, then for the new signer\*(Aqs own approval passphrase, twice; choose one different from the vault passphrase. The new signer alone can approve a config, so keep its passphrase apart from the first. Prints the new approver\*(Aqs ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault approver add\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-label\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enroll another approval signer. The service shows what changes, asks for the approval passphrase of an approver already pinned, then for the new signer\*(Aqs own approval passphrase, twice; choose one different from the vault passphrase. The new signer alone can approve a config, so keep its passphrase apart from the first. Prints the new approver\*(Aqs ID
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
What the approver is, 1 to 64 bytes: `backup passphrase`
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR [default: software]
The signer kind. Only `software` is offered so far; the service refuses the others
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
software: A key sealed to its own approval passphrase
.IP \(bu 2
tpm: A TPM approval key with a PIN
.IP \(bu 2
hardware: A hardware key with PIN and touch
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
